        {
          "type": "lowpass",
          "f": 1200,
          "q": 0.707
        }
      ],
      "why": "Euphonium from tenor trombone: tenor-tuba bore, much darker with a strong fundamental. Two cascaded 1.2 kHz low-passes (24 dB/oct) bring the harmonic centroid to 2.10 against 2.00 for real baritones (ChoraleBricks held-out songs, sounds/timbre_probe.py); the Iowa trombone stayed at 3.0 even with a 900 Hz 24 dB/oct low-pass.",
      "range": [
        34,
        74
      ],
      "extend": [
        {
          "library": "iowa-mis",
          "instrument": "tenor-trombone",
          "why": "VSCO tenor trombone stops at F4 (65); Iowa tenor trombone runs to C5 (72). Keys more than 2 semitones above the last VSCO note play Iowa samples, spectrally matched to the VSCO trombone on the 26 pitches both have, instead of a VSCO F4 stretched up to 9 semitones."
        }
      ]
