  "transposition": "Informational. Rendering consumes concert-pitch MIDI exported by MuseScore; targets are keyed at sounding pitch, so no transposition is applied at playback.",
  "band_soundfont": {
    "file": "data/sounds/band/brasscribe-band.sf2",
    "about": "One SoundFont for the whole band, built by sounds/band.py. Every brass part has its own sustain preset at (bank, program) and a staccato preset at (staccato_bank = bank + 64, program). The program is the part's General MIDI program from music/src/brasscribe_music/instruments.py (gm_program), so a GM player that ignores banks still plays the right family; bank 0 of each program is the section principal (Solo Cornet, 1st Trombone, E-flat Bass, Solo Horn), which is also what a bank-less lookup finds. Percussion is bank 128 program 0 on MIDI channel 10. MusicXML numbers are 1-based: <midi-program> = program + 1, <midi-bank> = bank + 1.",
    "layering": "A part whose players use more than one target (the cornet desks) layers those targets in its preset, detuned by +-3 cents, so one MIDI channel sounds like a section; the second voice adds about 3 dB, which channel_gain_db compensates.",
    "balance": "Part balance is applied as channel volume, not inside the SoundFont: channel_gain_db = gain_db - max(gain_db) - 3 dB if layered. Measured: AVAudioUnitSampler applies almost none of an SF2 preset-level initialAttenuation and FluidSynth 0.4 of it, so a balance baked into presets would differ per engine."
  },
  "lineups": {
    "about": "Every lineup the arranger writes (music/src/brasscribe_music/instruments.py, core/brasscribe-core/src/instruments.rs) and its score part names. sounds/checks.py coverage fails if any of these parts does not resolve to its own real-sample preset.",
    "Brass band": [
      "Soprano Cornet",
