  "balance": {
    "about": "parts[].balance_lu is the part's loudness as heard in the band at the same dynamic, in LU relative to the Solo Cornet section (whole desk, not one player). Every built target is levelled so its mf layer has the same K-weighted level (sounds/build.py TARGET_K_DB), so balance is only this number: apps set channel volume to channel_gain_db = balance_lu - max(balance_lu) - 3 dB for presets that layer two targets; the offline renderer sets each player to gain_db = balance_lu - 10 log10(players). sounds/checks.py balance measures it back from renders.",
    "rationale": "Brass-band practice: the solo cornets and the basses carry the band; soprano, repiano, flugel and solo horn sit about 3 LU under the solo cornets; the back-row cornets, horns and baritones lower again (4-6 LU), second parts 1 LU under firsts; trombones just under the cornets; the euphoniums (two players) are the second solo voice at -1; E♭ and B♭ basses (two each) at -1; percussion supports at -6. Heuristic, to be confirmed by listening with players."
  }
